zlib: Preserve _FILE_OFFSET_BITS when _TIME_BITS is defined

gzguts.h undefines _FILE_OFFSET_BITS when _LARGEFILE64_SOURCE is set. With
glibc time64 enabled, this causes compilation to fail because _TIME_BITS=64
requires _FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64. Keep _FILE_OFFSET_BITS defined in that case.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/gzguts.h
+++ b/gzguts.h
@@ -10,3 +10,3 @@
-#  ifdef _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
+#  if defined(_FILE_OFFSET_BITS) && !defined(_TIME_BITS)
 #    undef _FILE_OFFSET_BITS
 #  endif
